  "plain_text": "We had a virtual\nopening and more events coming ALL VIRTUAL EVENTS AND TICKETS HERE!\nTHE FUTURE EMERGENT\nvisual narratives for a planet in crisis and possibilityA PHYSICAL EXHIBITION, A WEBSITE OF IMAGERY AND SPECIAL ONLINE EVENTSFeaturing artists:\n,\nAmy Balkin, Lonny Brooks, The Bureau of Linguistic Reality, Kevin Cooley, Alan Clark, Delta_Ark, Serena Elston, Alicia Escott, David Huffman, Judit Navratil, Tiare Ribeaux, Malik Seneferu, Jody Stillwater, Kytana Winn, and Connie Zheng\nWe made a beautiful exhbit\nyou can see from window But we had to cancel scheduled visitsat\n349 15th Street Oakland CA 94612\n​Unfortunately we can not open the doors because there is just too much covid-19 spreading in Oakland and throughout California. We so believe in the righteous force of art but we also believe in science, the wisdom of public health in a pandemic and keeping each other safe. We have some creative means of seeing the work coming up so stay posted!Work by 14 artists suggests hints of sustenance as we live the unimaginable and seek radical possibility for the future. Weaving multiple strands, from an Afrofuturist vision to the algae fields of Hawaii to new seed pods in Northern California, we operate within the realm of speculative visioning: changing the way we experience the present by seeing present as past and practicing the future we want.\n​\nGO DEEPER INTO THE WORK\nWe have created another layer of seeing the Future Emergent in a special website of imagery, writings and musings EXPLORE THE FUTURE EMERGENT WEBSITE\nKytana Winn, and suddenly froze...: digital collage printed on Hahnemuhle Photo Rag, 2020Kevin Cooley, Magdalene Fjorden, digital chromogenic printAmy Balkin, The Atmosphere, A Guide, detail",
